      },
      "message": "fix(2d): close a near-end ring that owns no seam run\n\nThe seam ring''s reach gate admitted a boundary ring that stands near a\ncover end but owns no vertex on a bound. The split then found no seam\nrun and returned the ring open: its closing wall edge was dropped, and\nthe periodic copy did not restore it (PR #3496 review).\n\nA ring the gate admits now wraps the seam only when it carries a real\nseam run (a vertex on a cover bound) or spans a whole period of its own\nextent (the one-period band ring). A shorter near-end ring closes\nexactly as the no-seam path closes, so its wall ring survives.\n\nPinned by the_near_end_loop_without_a_seam_vertex_keeps_its_closing_edge;\nthe_wrapped_ring_cuts_no_azimuth_twice and\nthe_dflat_edge_walls_are_ringed stay green.\n\nRefs #3168",
